{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1541125-liminalities-in-other-media","id":1541125,"title":"Liminalities in Other Media","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-28T07:06:59-07:00","id":1541125,"title":"Liminalities in Other Media","content":"Trying to list out some Liminalities that might be present in Movies and TV shows. I probably have a few mistakes in here, but I thought this might be a fun exercise.<ul><li><b>Narnia</b> <b>Series </b>- Get access to Narnia through a cupboard.</li> <li><b>Old</b> - The beach where people age faster inside the beach than outside.</li> <li><b>The Cube</b> - Wake up to find a Shatter Spaced that is constantly moving and has traps everywhere, but the way to escape was not to move in the first place.</li> <li><b>13 Ghosts</b> - The building is an Interstitial Zone designed to keep Ghosts trapped inside.</li> <li><b>Evil </b>- The holes to Hell are Battlegrounds wherein the Demons can take physical form, but holy objects do not harm them. It is also where Hell (The Outside) is bleeding into reality.</li> <li><b>Escape Room</b> - Shattered spaces designed to feed off the deaths of the people who are tossed into them.</li> <li><b>Doctor Who</b> - So many, but definitely stuff like The God Complex where the Hotel is designed to feed on people's belief in a higher power, but if you don't have a belief in a higher power you can see the exit. Shattered Space.</li> <li><b>Red Dwarf</b> - Better Than Life is an Interstitial Zone that is trying to keep people inside it, so much so that it does Dreams Within Dreams to keep its users from logging off.</li> <li><b>Warehouse 13</b> - The Escher Vault is an Interstitial Zone used as storage for highly dangerous personal items from people who are &quot;Bronzed&quot;, a fate reserved for potential war criminals who use artificats.</li> <li><b>Superman</b> - The Phantom Zone is an Interstial Zone reservered for imprisoning the most dangerous criminals.</li> <li><b>Star Trek</b> - The Holodeck is a Liminality that can be shaped by the crew. In at least one case in Voyager, photon entities think the Holodeck is the crew of their ship and try to communicate with them, seeing the organic crew members as artificial life.</li> <li><b>Barbie Movie</b> - Barbie's world is connected to the real world via some sort of Liminality.</li> <li><b>Jumanji</b> - The board game acts as a conduit to allow the Jumanji world to bleed into our reality.</li> <li><b>Fringe </b>- The alternate reality tends to blend into the real world, with a stable bridge location at one point in the show where both realities can coexist.</li> <li><b>Severance</b> - The office building might be considered a Battleground in some way as the people who enter it are changed into their Inny self, a version of themself that only knows life in the office.</li> <li><b>Digimon Tamers</b> - Battlegrounds are created when the Digital World crosses over with reality creating these half digital half real zones where Digimon fight in the first half of the season.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T23:28:42-07:00","id":1541517,"title":"","content":"Not exactly mainstream TV or movies, but analog horror is a good source of both liminal spaces and Curseborne plot ideas. Just recently I watched The Oldest View. I'm planning on turning it into a Curseborne story once we get a more complete set of rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}